{{!-- ONE ENTRY ON THE TIMELINE.

      The same card on all three hosts: the tab, the aggregate window, and the journal page a track
      reads back as. It differs only by `canEdit`, which the view model already answered per track,
      so no host decides for itself who may write here.

      A card with no title is not a broken card. An entry is a dated thing that happened, and the
      account is the part that matters; the title is a line to find it by. So the head renders only
      what there is, and a titleless entry reads as its body under its date.

      An AUTO card is one the system wrote for itself (a season turning, a level gained, a kill)
      rather than one somebody typed. It wears its KIND as a chip, glyph AND word, at full ink: a
      reader on a magnifier must never have to guess what a row is from an icon or a faint badge.
      Typed cards wear no chip; their words are the whole of them.

      An auto card also wears its kind's COLOUR (`stonetop-timeline-kind--<kind>`), on the edge, the
      spine dot and the chip's rim and glyph, never on a word. The colour is the second way the kind
      is said; the chip's word is the first, for the readers at this table who cannot tell the
      colours apart. A GM can repaint a kind for the world from the toolbar.

      A TYPED card wearing a TAG (`isTagged`, timeline-tags.js) wears the same chip and colour: a
      borrowed kind's, or a custom tag's name with its colour handed in `kindStyle`, one value per
      skin, which the `stonetop-timeline-kind--custom` rules choose from.

      A KILLS card prints who fell ("Crinwin ×3, Bandit Chief") above whatever note the table added.

      Context: one card view-model (timeline-view.js#cardVM), plus `enrichedBody` where the host has
      enriched it. --}}
<li class="stonetop-timeline-card{{#if isAuto}} stonetop-timeline-card--auto stonetop-timeline-kind--{{this.kind}}{{/if}}{{#if isTagged}} stonetop-timeline-card--tagged stonetop-timeline-kind--{{this.kind}}{{/if}}"{{#if kindStyle}} style="{{this.kindStyle}}"{{/if}} data-entry-id="{{this.id}}">
	{{#if wearsChip}}
	<span class="stonetop-timeline-card-kind">
		<i class="fas {{this.kindIcon}}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
		<span>{{this.kindLabel}}</span>
	</span>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if title}}
	<h4 class="stonetop-timeline-card-title">{{this.title}}</h4>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if killSummary}}
	<p class="stonetop-timeline-card-kills">{{this.killSummary}}</p>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if place}}
	<p class="stonetop-timeline-card-place">
		<i class="fas fa-location-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i>
		{{#if placeLinked}}
		{{!-- A place that IS a document, dropped on the field when the entry was written.

		      ⚠ ALL THREE OF `class`, `data-link` AND `draggable` ARE LOAD-BEARING, and only the
		      middle one actually does anything. Core binds content links on document.body with
		      `event.target.closest("a[data-link]")` and then reads `.dataset.uuid` off that same
		      element; `content-link` is the LOOK alone. A link with the class and the uuid but no
		      `data-link` renders perfectly, carries the right target, and silently does nothing when
		      clicked, with no console error. --}}
		<a class="content-link" data-link data-uuid="{{this.placeUuid}}" draggable="true">{{this.place}}</a>
		{{else}}
		<span>{{this.place}}</span>
		{{/if}}
	</p>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if enrichedBody}}
	<div class="stonetop-timeline-card-body">{{{this.enrichedBody}}}</div>
	{{/if}}

	{{#if canEdit}}
	<div class="stonetop-timeline-card-actions">
		<button type="button" class="stonetop-timeline-move" data-entry-id="{{this.id}}" data-delta="-1"
		        aria-label="{{localize "stonetop.timeline.moveEarlier"}}"
		        data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.timeline.moveEarlier"}}"
		        data-tooltip-direction="UP"><i class="fas fa-chevron-up"></i></button>
		<button type="button" class="stonetop-timeline-move" data-entry-id="{{this.id}}" data-delta="1"
		        aria-label="{{localize "stonetop.timeline.moveLater"}}"
		        data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.timeline.moveLater"}}"
		        data-tooltip-direction="UP"><i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></button>
		<button type="button" class="stonetop-timeline-edit" data-entry-id="{{this.id}}"
		        aria-label="{{localize "stonetop.timeline.editEntry"}}"
		        data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.timeline.editEntry"}}"
		        data-tooltip-direction="UP"><i class="fas fa-pen"></i></button>
		<button type="button" class="stonetop-timeline-remove" data-entry-id="{{this.id}}"
		        aria-label="{{localize "stonetop.timeline.removeEntry"}}"
		        data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.timeline.removeEntry"}}"
		        data-tooltip-direction="UP"><i class="fas fa-xmark"></i></button>
	</div>
	{{/if}}
</li>
